# Git Workflow Standards

- Branch names must be one of:
  - `feat/*`, `fix/*`, `chore/*`, `docs/*`, `refactor/*`, `test/*`, `ci/*`, `release/*`, `hotfix/*`
- Do not push direct feature work to `main` or `master`.
- Commit messages must follow Conventional Commits (`type(scope): summary`).
- Never append `Made-with: Cursor` (or any similar Cursor/tooling attribution line) to commit messages unless the user explicitly asks.
- Prefer `npm run commit` (Commitizen) for consistent commit metadata.
- PRs must include summary, reason, test plan, and risk notes.
- Keep commits scoped and atomic; avoid unrelated changes in one commit.
- Ensure checks pass before requesting review:
  - `npm run type-check`
  - `npm run lint` when stable/non-interactive
  - Run `npm run build` only when the user explicitly requests it or before a release/merge that requires it

